==English==

===Alternative forms===
* (''Commonwealth spelling'') [[fervour]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|fervor||a boiling or raging heat, heat, vehemence, passion}}, from {{m|la|fervere||to boil, be hot}}; see [[fervent]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/ˈfɝvɚ/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-fervor.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|US}} An [[intense]], [[heated]] [[emotion]]; [[passion]], [[ardor]].
# {{lb|en|US}} A [[passionate]] [[enthusiasm]] for some cause.
# {{lb|en|US}} [[heat|Heat]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|passionate enthusiasm}} {{l|en|fire in the belly}}, {{l|en|zeal}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|fervent}}
* {{l|en|fervid}}
* {{l|en|fever}}

